    <static seed="2" source="Library/WHFreeman/Holt_linear_algebra/Chaps_1-4/3.3.54.pg">
      <statement><p>Solve for the matrix <m>X</m> if <m>AX(D+B X)^{-1} = C</m>. Assume that all matrices are <m>n\times n</m> and invertible as needed.</p>
<p><m>X =</m><fillin name="AnSwEr0001" characters="10"/></p>
</statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>\left(A-CB\right)^{-1}CD</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <solution><p><alert>SOLUTION:</alert> 
Note that
<me>\begin{align*}
AX(D+BX)^{-1} = C \amp \Rightarrow AX = C(D+BX) = CD + CBX \\
\amp \Rightarrow  AX - CBX = CD\\
\amp \Rightarrow (A-CB)X = CD \\
\amp \Rightarrow X = (A-CB)^{-1} CD.
\end{align*}</me></p>
</solution>
